{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>He shall carry forth outside the camp</b> — \"He shall carry forth\" refers to Aaron, who was mentioned (in verses 23, 25), given as a command, according to the opinion of R. Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Leviticus 16:27). But the correct interpretation is that \"he shall carry forth\" means the one who carries forth. And likewise, \"and they shall burn\" means those who burn. Scripture said \"and they shall burn\" in plural language, to teach that if many people engaged in the burning — one brings the fire, one arranges the wood of the pile, and one kindles the fire — they do not defile their garments, but rather only the one who sets the fire to the bulls themselves, from the time he ignites the majority of it. Therefore Scripture went back and said in singular language, \"and he who burns them\"."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:54:30.118584477Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}